  "all_ingredients_flat": "brown rice flour, sorghum flour, water, chilli powder, sesame seeds, ajwain (carom seeds), turmeric, black pepper, flaxseed powder, salt",
  "instructions": "(1) Boil water in a pan. Slowly add all the ingredients except flour.\n(2) Once water comes to boil, add 1 cup of flour, cook for a minute. Then switch off the stove and cover the pan with a lid.\n(3) Preheat the air fryer.\n(4) With wet hands, mix the dough. Make small balls and roll them into small cylinders, shape them into rings.\n(5) Place these rings in the air fryer for 6-8 minutes at 350F. Check after 6 minutes. Cook until they are crunchy.",
